    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling output today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our premier efficiency score of 81.88. Facing Reynaldo L\u00f3pez, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive park factor boost and a favorable platoon dynamic, making him an elite start at shortstop. Close behind, **Drake Baldwin** (71.83) and **Jackson Merrill** (71.56) represent the strongest secondary plays. **Drake Baldwin** is buoyed by favorable park dimensions and projected leadoff duties, while **Jackson Merrill** draws a high-upside matchup against Janson Junk, capitalizing on a significant SP skill advantage. We are also looking for meaningful production from **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (66.73); despite the tough matchup against Ranger Suarez, his elite talent profile overcomes the SP skill deficit to remain a must-start staple.\n\nThe decision-making process for the utility and outfield slots was dictated by our aggressive weight on speed and favorable park factors. **Dominic Smith** (62.63) cracked the lineup because his matchup against Shane Baz provides a massive 16% park boost, whereas **Denzer Guzman** was the toughest omission from the starting nine. While **Denzer Guzman** posted an attractive 53.32 score against Carson Whisenhunt\u2014aided by a significant boost for the pitcher's poor xERA\u2014he ultimately fell short due to the lack of a locked-in lineup spot and lower relative efficiency compared to the high-floor production of **Jacob Wilson** (62.27) and **Andy Pages** (61.31). \n\nRisks remain present across the board as every projected lineup is currently pending official release. **Heliot Ramos** (54.55) carries the most situational complexity today; his score is dragged down by his tendency to hold runners and the presence of an elite catcher, though he is salvaged by a wind-out advantage that could lead to a sudden spike in power production. We will continue to monitor the status of **Kyle Tucker**, whose score of 64.35 reflects a high base projection that remains robust even against the moderate difficulty of Freddy Peralta. Owners should keep a close eye on the confirmed lineups, as any shift from our assumed batting orders for **Nasim Nunez** or **Curtis Mead** could necessitate a quick pivot to our bench depth.",
